    "license": "Project-authored original parametric source adaptation from company-makeup-mirror-v1. No external art/model input. Three.js 0.187.0 is MIT licensed.",
    "prompt": "Purpose: four real wall-mounted makeup mirrors, targetProfileId makeup-mirror-wall, targetProfileVersion 1. Adapt the pinned project-authored tabletop heads in metres, +Y up and +Z toward the room. Remove base/post, translate retained vertices by [0,-.365,.038], add a closed .16 x .24 x .02m mounting plate with back Z=0, retain finite pane contours and fixed three-plane wings. Preserve wall mounting, warm-white spotlight and separate emissive housing. Bake identity transforms. Budget 2500 triangles/32 meshes/four materials. The measured Kenney candidate lacks the required pane and lamp mapping. Rebuild through the pinned exporter and validate actual loaded GLBs through the independent gate. Record source identities, frame edit, failures and limits. Design: Adapt pinned arch mirror head, retain original contours and material, rigid transform plus closed wall plate. An actual .34m wide arch with straight lower sides, bottom at Y=.18m, upper arc centre Y=.38m and top Y=.55m. Use 24 upper-arc segments, a matching solid back and continuous metal ring.",
    "sourceDesign": "arch",
    "method": "Adapted pinned original mirror head with base/post removed, rigidly translated vertices and a new closed wall mounting plate. Finite convex pane contours and distinct tri-fold plane transforms are baked into Float32 resource-space vertices. Deterministic GLTFExporter with actual GLTFLoader readback and independent makeup-mirror geometry admission.",
    "limitations": [
      "Arched top is a finite 24-segment arc. No bending or deformation state.",
      "Wall-mounted source adaptation. Real wall/reflection/illumination require separate runtime evidence."
    ]
